.TH CRUNCH_RESTART_SYSCALL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
crunch_restart_syscall \- invokes the internal linux restart_syscall entry point
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_extra.h>
.B long crunch_restart_syscall(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes the internal Linux restart_syscall entry point. It is intended for kernel signal-restart machinery, not ordinary application calls.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR restart_syscall (2)
